# Every checkout must materialize identical bytes on every platform. GitHub's
# Windows runners check out with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrote LICENSE to
# CRLF; scripts/stage-distribution-legal.sh then copied those bytes into the
# Windows release zip while the four tarballs carried LF. The v6.4.8 release
# job failed at "LICENSE differs in ...windows-msvc.zip.d" only after all five
# native targets, the component job, and the crates.io publication had already
# succeeded. No tracked file carries a CR byte; pin that so no checkout can add
# one. Overrides below win because later patterns take precedence.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Append-only audit ledger: union-merge so a lane branch merge can never
# drop a sibling lane's verdict rows (#261).
.shepherd/runs/*/auditor-verdicts.txt merge=union

# These files are named by the SHA-256 of their exact upstream bytes. Treat
# them as binary so Git never rewrites line endings or flags an upstream
# license's whitespace as authored source drift.
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/*.txt binary
